We have the system of equations:
\begin{align*}
4u - 5v &= 23 \quad \text{(1)} \\
2u + 4v &= -8 \quad \text{(2)}
\end{align*}
To eliminate one of the variables, we can multiply equation (2) by 2 to get:
\begin{align*}
4u + 8v &= -16 \quad \text{(3)}
\end{align*}
Now, we can subtract equation (1) from equation (3) to eliminate $u$:
\begin{align*}
(4u + 8v) - (4u - 5v) &= -16 - 23 \\
13v &= -39 \\
v &= -3
\end{align*}
Substituting this value of $v$ back into equation (1) to solve for $u$:
\begin{align*}
4u - 5(-3) &= 23 \\
4u + 15 &= 23 \\
4u &= 8 \\
u &= 2
\end{align*}
Finally, we can find the value of $u + v$:
\begin{align*}
u + v &= 2 + (-3) \\
u + v &= -1
\end{align*}
Therefore, the value of $u + v$ is $\boxed{-1}$.

